casebook centrifugal-pump-conditions v4
source "FMEA-PUMP-001 rev C" dated 2026-03-14 by "J. Okafor"
note "CONTROLLED EXPERIMENT. pump.cb plus CONDITION claims and nothing else, so the difference is attributable."
note ""
note "pump.cb diagnoses well and responds badly. Every claim in it is `needs A B` -- two coinciding symptoms --"
note "because it was designed for DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS: telling cavitation from bearing wear from misalignment."
note "Comparing it against ordinary prioritised alarm annunciation showed what that costs. A pump with a hot"
note "bearing and nothing else asserted gets `continue`, while the alarm system it would replace says `shutdown`."
note "All 14 single symptoms produce no response whatsoever."
note ""
note "The missing distinction is between a DIAGNOSIS and a CONDITION. `bearing_wear` is a hypothesis about a"
note "cause and needs corroboration before anyone acts on it. `bearing running hot` is not a hypothesis -- it is"
note "a damaging state of affairs, it is damaging whatever the cause, and waiting for a second symptom means"
note "waiting for the damage. Both belong in a casebook, and pump.cb only had the first kind."
note ""
note "Vibration alone classifies at roughly 89%; vibration with motor stator current at roughly 97%."
note "Dominant nuisance-alarm cause is benign duty-point change, not sensor noise."

# ─── what the instruments report ────────────────────────────────────────────
observe vib_high          "broadband vibration above alarm threshold"
observe vib_1x            "1x running speed dominant"
observe vib_bpf           "blade-pass-frequency harmonics present"
observe bearing_temp_high "bearing temperature elevated"
observe suction_low       "suction pressure low, NPSH margin eroded"
observe head_low          "developed head below curve"
observe crackling         "audible vapour-bubble implosion"
observe duty_changed      "duty point changed"
observe throttled         "discharge throttled"
observe near_critical     "running speed near a structural critical"
observe mount_suspect     "accelerometer mount integrity questioned"
observe calib_overdue     "instrument calibration past due"
observe current_broadband "stator current broadband modulation"
observe current_sidebands "stator current blade-pass sidebands"

# Two-phase flow is stochastic, a geometric defect is shaft-locked. A real spectrum cannot
# show both, so if both appear the instrument is at fault -- the compiler generates that doubt.
exclusive current_broadband current_sidebands

# ─── diagnoses ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
claim cavitation      "impeller cavitation"        needs vib_high suction_low
claim bearing_wear    "bearing degradation"        needs vib_high bearing_temp_high
claim impeller_defect "impeller geometric wear"    needs vib_high vib_bpf
claim misalignment    "shaft misalignment"         needs vib_high vib_1x

# ─── conditions: damaging states of affairs, not hypotheses about causes ────
# Each needs ONE observation, because each IS the thing that matters rather than evidence for it. Still defeasible: a
# discredited instrument is discredited whatever it is measuring, and `calib_stale` already undermines these readings.

# A hot bearing damages the bearing regardless of why it is hot. Waiting for vibration to confirm it means waiting for
# the damage the temperature was warning about.
claim bearing_hot "bearing temperature elevated, cause not yet distinguished" severity 7 needs bearing_temp_high

# Audible vapour-bubble implosion is not evidence OF cavitation, it is cavitation, happening now, removing metal.
claim cavitating_now "vapour bubbles are collapsing in the pump now" severity 8 needs crackling

# NPSH margin eroded is a damaging operating condition in its own right: it is the state that produces cavitation, and
# it is actionable before any vibration signature appears.
claim npsh_eroded "suction conditions outside the pump's NPSH requirement" severity 6 needs suction_low

# A duty change raises load and therefore bearing temperature, and it changes the operating point away from the curve.
# So it undercuts the temperature and NPSH conditions -- but NOT `cavitating_now`, because a duty change does not make
# metal-removing implosion acceptable.
duty_change undercuts bearing_hot npsh_eroded

# ─── benign explanations, which are what suppress nuisance alarms ───────────
excuse duty_change "pump changed duty point"    needs duty_changed
excuse offdesign   "running off design point"   needs throttled
excuse resonance   "structural resonance"       needs near_critical

# ─── reasons to distrust the instruments ────────────────────────────────────
doubt mount_loose "accelerometer mount loose" needs mount_suspect
  undermines vib_high vib_1x vib_bpf

doubt calib_stale "calibration stale" needs calib_overdue
  undermines vib_high bearing_temp_high current_broadband current_sidebands

# ─── how the evidence discriminates ─────────────────────────────────────────
# A live benign explanation defeats the inference to a fault.
duty_change undercuts cavitation impeller_defect misalignment
offdesign   undercuts cavitation
resonance   undercuts misalignment bearing_wear

# Discriminating evidence defeats the benign explanation, reinstating the fault.
suction_low       rebuts duty_change offdesign
head_low          rebuts duty_change
bearing_temp_high rebuts resonance
crackling         rebuts resonance offdesign impeller_defect
misalignment      rebuts resonance

# Cavitation and impeller wear both destroy head. With no discriminator the honest answer is
# "cannot tell", and mutual rebuttal is how that is said.
cavitation      rebuts impeller_defect
impeller_defect rebuts cavitation

# The current channel breaks that deadlock, in whichever direction the spectrum points.
current_broadband rebuts impeller_defect
current_sidebands rebuts cavitation

# ─── what to do ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
action continue idle
action maintain when any cavitation bearing_wear impeller_defect misalignment bearing_hot npsh_eroded
# `cavitating_now` joins shutdown, not maintain: damage is being done at this moment, and severity 8 says so.
action shutdown safe when any bearing_wear cavitating_now
prefer shutdown over maintain over continue
